  "character": "The French Riviera of the Alps. Refined, historic, built by the Rothschilds in the 1920s. Elegant chalet architecture, Michelin-starred dining, luxury boutiques.",
  "description": "Megeve was built in the 1920s as a winter playground for European aristocracy \u2014 the Rothschild family created it as an alternative to St Moritz. It has genuine old-town charm, cobbled streets, a central square with a 12th-century church, horse-drawn carriages, and some of the best dining in the Alps (including Flocons de Sel \u2014 3 Michelin stars). The skiing is across two mountain sectors (Rochebrune and Mont d'Arbois) linked with Saint-Gervais for 325km total. Golf course in summer.",
